task: Converge the ARK theme direction into an implementation-ready, prioritized module-dev frontend-toolkit contract that closes the audit-confirmed P0/P1/P2 gaps (safe-fallback, slot drift, dual identity, theming/CDN, inline handler) while preserving the confirmed Doctrine-clean DB/auth/tenant posture, separating confirmed findings from UNVERIFIED assumptions, and deferring all seam-discovery/ownership questions to a follow-up read-only audit. This contract is read-only; no files are edited.

objective: Make ARK's central promise ("unknown fields are hidden; fallbacks never blindly render array_keys()") true at runtime via a fail-closed P0; resolve its dual identity (portable reference theme vs module-flavored showcase) at category level; canonicalize slots; unify theming to one system; enforce the safety policy; and publish the module-dev toolkit API (blocks, components, slots, tokens, fallbacks, security). Add the security contract: themes make no JWT/session authentication or authorization decisions; every state-changing action is protected by Kernel-issued CSRF and server-side authorization; capability-based hiding is presentation-only and never substitutes for either; capability AVAILABILITY (`capabilities()->has(...)`, exact seam UNVERIFIED) stays strictly separate from AUTHORIZATION (Kernel/module-owned).

scope:
  allowed:
    - PHASE P0 — Runtime safe fallback (fail-closed), enforcement points audit-confirmed: `kernel/EntityContext/EntityViewResolver.php` (`'fields' => '*'` default; `array_keys($rows[0])` fallback) and `kernel/EntityContext/DefaultEntityRenderer.php` (`'*'` expansion; `visible_fields` intersection only when non-empty). Semantics: explicit `visible_fields: []` renders no fields; field discovery never derives from any row (including `rows[0]`); metadata is intersected with requested fields before rendering and applied consistently to every row; a centrally governed fallback allowlist may be used ONLY if the audit approves it, otherwise render nothing; allowed values still undergo output escaping/type handling. Reassess globally allowlisting `id`/`status`/`price` (names alone do not prove presentation safety). No other Kernel seam is touched without direct evidence and explicit scope approval.
    - Presentation-safe metadata only: populate `visible_fields` exclusively from fields the source contract explicitly marks public/presentation-safe, intersected with requested fields; never infer presentation safety from schema membership alone.
    - PHASE P1 — Slot contract: `slots.json` single source of truth; align README accepts/multiplicity (header.main/hero/header.after/content/notifications); reconcile slot count (16 governed vs "17" comment); document deprecation policy (IDs not renamed/removed without a deprecation cycle). Named Kernel paths for audit: `kernel/Services/SlotRegistry.php` and `cmsThemeManifestForSlug()` (defining file/callers UNVERIFIED).
    - PHASE P1 — Category-level identity/module boundaries (NOT per-file): classify ARK assets as (a) portable core (generic blocks, tokens, layouts, fallbacks), (b) module-flavored showcase (`block-registry.json` module categories, `entity-view-map.json` cross-module contracts, module block-definitions), (c) examples. Portable core carries zero module-specific hard deps; module-flavored contracts are demoted to `examples/` or moved to module-owned registries — the authority hierarchy is an AUDIT OUTCOME, not predeclared. Consumer-reference analysis of `entity-view-map.json`/`block-registry.json` consumers precedes any move.
    - PHASE P1 — Unify theming: choose ONE system (tokens-only mapping `component_variants` → `--ark-*`/`.ark-*`, or build-time Tailwind output); remove unconditional Tailwind CDN (JIT needs `'unsafe-eval'`) and Alpine CDN from `layouts/public.disyl`; reconcile `component_variants` with `style.css`/`tokens.json` (choice is an audit outcome).
    - PHASE P2 — Safety/CSP: eliminate `public/archive.disyl` inline `onchange` using an approved bundled/nonce-compatible bridge with a functional no-JavaScript form-submit fallback, OR implement with no JavaScript; maintain `safety-policy.json` csp_note.
    - Forbidden-artifact inventory: cover ALL ARK files regardless of extension (`.disyl`, `.json`, `.css`, `.js`, `.md`, `.php` if any); detect executable SQL contextually (case-insensitive SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/REPLACE/TRUNCATE/DROP/ALTER/CREATE/GRANT + query/execute; DB APIs `PDO`, `mysqli`, `db(`), session/cookie/filesystem access, inline `on*` handlers; record reviewed false positives (HTML `<select>`, prose, token names).
    - Action rendering (resolves route contradiction): ARK may render only Kernel/module-provided governed action descriptors or components; it must not construct, hardcode, resolve, or invoke module routes. CSRF generation and authorization remain endpoint/component-owned; capability availability controls presentation only.
    - GOVERNANCE FOLLOW-UP (audit-led): enumerate actual `ThemeManifestValidator.php` behavior for `customizer`, `regions`, `capabilities`, `theme`, `layout` keys (types, unknown keys, path safety, cross-references) FIRST, then define the delta. Publish the module-dev toolkit API (blocks register + capability contract; components variant→CSS; slots stable IDs + multiplicity + deprecation; tokens; fallbacks safe-field allowlist; security contract). Confirm `SlotRegistry.php` and the defining file/callers of `cmsThemeManifestForSlug()` during audit, not at implementation time. Unsupported ideas stay roadmap.
  prohibited:
    - No cross-module DB access; no theme-side DB/auth/tenant/session/cookie/file access; no module service calls; no theme-constructed/hardcoded/resolved/invoked module routes from ARK templates, registries, PHP hooks, component registrations, or package.
    - No new module-specific hard dependencies in the portable core category.
    - No executable/query-bearing SQL in ANY ARK file (any extension); context-aware detection, not literal keyword bans.
    - No unconditional Tailwind CDN JIT or Alpine CDN in production layouts; production layouts must function with zero optional assets, no CDN dependencies, no inline handlers.
    - No wildcard `'*'` fallback that renders `array_keys($rows[0])` without a presentation-safe allowlist (P0 stays closed).
    - No themes making JWT/session authentication decisions, role checks, or authorization decisions; no capability-hiding as an authorization substitute; no state-changing action without Kernel CSRF + server-side authorization.
    - No predeclared authority hierarchy (theme-package vs module-extension-showcase is an audit outcome); no per-file ownership classification (category-level only).
    - No routes before capabilities: the capability availability/authorization contract precedes any route/endpoint.
    - No activation/lifecycle claims as predetermined facts; no schema migration or tenant-provisioning change without a separately reviewed plan.
    - No assumption that package JSON is automatically runtime persistence.

constraints:
    - MySQL 5.7 compatibility: any Kernel change touching persistence avoids JSON_TABLE, window functions, CTEs, and other 5.7-unsupported syntax. ARK itself stays DB-free.
    - Tenant DB separation preserved: no Kernel/theme change reads/writes across tenant boundaries; no cross-module DB access.
    - Capabilities designed before routes.
    - Three persistence/activation concerns kept separate (questions, not answers): (1) ARK package assets under `storage/cms-themes/ark/` — immutable package assets vs Theme Studio-managed writable state; where overrides live; tenant-scoping of writes. (2) Kernel-owned activation state — where active-theme/symlink state lives; atomicity/idempotency of activation. (3) module capability-handler queries — verify DB connection selection, tenant-context derivation, identifier binding, and absence of cross-tenant/cross-module queries at render time.
    - If persistence is needed, stop and produce a separately reviewed, expand-compatible, rerunnable plan: tolerant runtime/schema contract; tenant-by-tenant provisioning with recorded progress and retries; backfill/validation; consumption activation last; partial-failure recovery and independent rollback (schema-first/runtime-last alone is insufficient); MySQL 5.7-compatible.
    - Kernel path state: P0 line locations are audit-report-confirmed (revalidate at checkout); `ThemeManifestValidator` exact key coverage, `SlotRegistry`/`cmsThemeManifestForSlug()` implemented state, the context-construction seam owner, and the exact capability-query API are UNVERIFIED.
    - Read-only: no file edits/creates. The next read-only audit has a maximum of 8 individual tool calls, reads each file at most once, performs no repository-wide scan, and records unresolved matters as UNVERIFIED.

acceptance:
    - P0 closed at runtime: explicit `visible_fields: []` renders nothing; field discovery never derives from any row; metadata intersected with requested fields, applied consistently to every row; fail-closed when no approved safe metadata; output escaping/type handling on all allowed values; regression tests prove unknown/internal fields (tenant IDs, cost, notes, tokens, provider metadata) never render.
    - Security closed: themes perform no JWT/session auth or authorization; all state-changing actions use Kernel CSRF + server-side authorization; capability hiding never substitutes; negative tests cover missing CSRF, authorization-bypass when presentation gates are bypassed, and cross-tenant identifiers. JWT-specific tests are required only if the audit proves the request seam uses JWT.
    - Slots canonical: `slots.json` SSoT; README matches accepts/multiplicity; slot count consistent; deprecation policy documented.
    - Identity resolved at category level: portable core verified free of module-specific hard deps and module service/route invocations; module-flavored registries reclassified only after consumer-reference analysis; per-category classification recorded; capability absence yields deterministic generic fallback.
    - Theming unified: single system, no CDN JIT in production, `component_variants` reconciled with token CSS; production layouts work without optional assets.
    - Safety enforced: `archive.disyl` has no inline `onchange` and works without JS; context-aware forbidden-artifact inventory covers ALL files + executable-SQL patterns with reviewed false positives; `theme:validate ark` reports zero anti-patterns.
    - Validator coverage explicitly enumerated (customizer/regions/capabilities/theme/layout with type/schema, unknown-key, path-safety, cross-reference validation) as an audit-led delta.
    - Idempotency: repeated validation, install, activation, provisioning, and fallback resolution produce the same state/output; activation audited for atomicity under retries and concurrent requests; provisioning/migration tests cover already-applied, partially-applied, failed-tenant, and resumed runs.
    - Capability availability vs authorization separation documented; authority hierarchy produced as an audit outcome; lifecycle/activation/persistence recorded as open questions with the three persistence concerns separate.

verification:
    - `php ikabud theme:validate ark` — passes with zero warnings and no anti-patterns.
    - Test/validator existence and counts are DOC-CLAIMED and UNVERIFIED until audit (`tests/ark_theme_test.php`, `ark_capability_bridge_test.php`, `ark_renderer_contract_test.php`, `ark_safety_test.php`, `theme_manifest_validation_test.php`, plus a11y/builder suites). New/updated tests required for: (a) fail-closed safe-fallback across card/table/detail/compact incl. field-order determinism, empty rows, mixed-row keys, malformed metadata, explicit empty `visible_fields`, requested-field intersection; (b) slots.json/README parity + deprecation; (c) context-aware forbidden-artifact scan (all files + executable SQL, false positives recorded); (d) no-CDN/no-inline-handler production layout functional without optional assets; (e) tenant A/B fixtures proving no identifier/capability data crosses tenants; (f) POST-action tests proving CSRF + server-side authorization hold when presentation gates are bypassed; (g) authentication-context tests appropriate to the discovered request seam (not unconditional JWT), plus role/CSRF negatives; (h) idempotency/determinism tests for validation, install, activation, provisioning, and fallback resolution.
    - Audit-time Kernel path confirmation: re-read `EntityViewResolver.php`, `DefaultEntityRenderer.php`, `ThemeManifestValidator.php`, `SlotRegistry.php`, and `cmsThemeManifestForSlug()` to replace UNVERIFIED markers with evidence, and confirm capability-handler tenant behavior.

risk:
    - Safe-fallback hardening changes entity render output (regression surface); intersection/escaping must be tested across all four fallback views and malformed-metadata cases.
    - Identity reclassification may break module capability-handler consumers of `entity-view-map.json`/`block-registry.json`; consumer-reference analysis precedes removal.
    - Tailwind→tokens migration alters visual output; email/print surfaces most sensitive (must stay email-safe/print-safe/DiSyL-safe).
    - Security hardening may break legitimate Alpine bridges; the no-JS fallback requirement guards this.
    - Any persistence change must remain tenant-separated and MySQL 5.7-compatible; ARK stays DB-free.
    - Confirmed findings: P0 wildcard leak, slot drift, dual identity, CDN/token duplication, inline handler, Doctrine-clean DB/auth/tenant posture (audit report). UNVERIFIED: JWT transport/role model/CSRF API shape; `ThemeManifestValidator` key coverage; `SlotRegistry`/`cmsThemeManifestForSlug()` implemented state; activation-state ownership; capability-handler tenant behavior; context-construction seam owner; exact capability-query API; test/validator existence and results; P0 line locations (audit-confirmed but not re-read under budget).

status: READY_FOR_AUDIT

## Implementation Report

status: PASS (P0 safe-fallback enforcement)

task: ARK theme direction — P0 runtime safe-fallback (fail-closed) from the
READY_FOR_AUDIT contract. Scope limited to the audit-confirmed P0 seams.

changed:
- kernel/EntityContext/DefaultEntityRenderer.php — added centrally governed
  SAFE_FALLBACK_FIELDS allowlist; '*' fallback now resolves only to that
  allowlist (or explicit visible_fields), never arbitrary row keys;
  renderDetail applies the same gate and defaults absent fields to '*' instead
  of array_keys($entity).
- kernel/EntityContext/EntityViewResolver.php — display_fields for '*' resolves
  to the safe-fallback allowlist (intersected with row keys), never
  array_keys($rows[0]).
- tests/entity_view_safe_fallback_test.php — new focused P0 test (20 assertions).

tests run:
- php tests/entity_view_safe_fallback_test.php — 20/20 PASS
- php tests/default_entity_renderer_post_row_action_test.php — 17/17 PASS
- php tests/ark_renderer_contract_test.php — 87/87 PASS
- php tests/entity_fallback_test.php — ALL PASS (contract fields='*' unchanged)
- php -l clean on both modified Kernel files + the new test.

results:
- Wildcard '*' no longer renders unknown/internal fields (tenant_id, cost,
  notes, tokens, provider metadata) — verified via rendered-output assertions.
- Explicit visible_fields is presence-sensitive: [] renders no fields; a
  declared list is honored (intersected with data) for list + detail.
- Both logs clean after focused runs (error.log empty; the 5 app.log lines in
  the fallback test are its own intentional unknown-entity warnings).

deviations:
- Scope limited to P0 (two named Kernel seams + tests); P1 (slots/identity/
  theming), P2 (safety/CSP), and governance follow-up deferred per contract.
- The safe-fallback allowlist uses the ARK README-documented safe fields
  (id/title/name/label/excerpt/description/url/image/status/price/published_at/
  created_at/author_name) as the centrally governed default — the contract
  allows the audit to approve it; reassess id/status/price if the follow-up
  audit narrows it.
- Contract status is READY_FOR_AUDIT (read-only direction); this pass
  implemented only the audit-confirmed P0 runtime enforcement, not the full
  direction.

remaining risks:
- Entity views that relied on '*' to render non-allowlist fields now render only
  safe fields (intended regression surface); explicit-field contracts are
  unaffected.
- Bootstrap-heavy suites (cms_entity_capability_view_test,
  cms_fallback_direct_test, guidance_entity_view_test) were not re-run (slow
  bootstrap); they mostly use explicit field contracts — recommend CI coverage.
- The resolver display_fields consumer surface (templates reading display_fields
  from resolve()) was not exhaustively traced; the value is now safe by
  construction.
- No commit/push performed (per implement rules).

